# Both images (cmd/bigfleet/Dockerfile, test/scaletest/image/Dockerfile)
# build from the repo root with `COPY . .`. Without this file the build
# context is ~1.7GB and — worse — every scaletest run writes into
# test/scaletest/results/ inside the context, so the NEXT run's
# byte-identical source still invalidates the COPY layer and rebuilds +
# kind-reloads images for nothing (measured: 22s + 3s per gate run).
# Excluding the non-build trees makes image digests a pure function of
# the source tree, which the digest-verification discipline (M47.7)
# wants anyway.
#
# Keep: all Go source, go.mod/go.sum, api/crd/ (CRD bundle COPY),
# test/scaletest/image/*.sh (entrypoint COPYs).
.git/
test/scaletest/results/
site/
bin/
node_modules/
docs/
coverage*
/bigfleet
/scaletest-runner
*.log
.claude/
